Alpha-stage R8/GR16/BGR24 TEV compares read the stage's colour inputs

GameCube behaviour: in an alpha TEV stage, GX_TEV_COMP_R8_*, GX_TEV_COMP_GR16_* and
GX_TEV_COMP_BGR24_* compare the colour channels (R, GR, BGR) of the stage's colour
inputs A and B, then select the alpha input C (or zero) and add D. Only
GX_TEV_COMP_A8_* (== RGB8) compares the alpha inputs. Dolphin models this with tevin_a /
tevin_b, which hold the colour inputs in .rgb and the alpha inputs in .a, as read at the
start of the stage.

Aurora 3227d76 passed the scalar alpha inputs to tev_op, which emits `<a>.r`, `<a>.rg`
or `<a>.rgb` and so builds invalid WGSL ("cannot index into expression of type f32"),
aborting in aurora::gx::build_shader (the game, sea room 44). The fix latches the
stage's colour inputs A and B into `let` locals before the colour result is written and
uses them for those three compares in the alpha half.

Upstream status: not reported upstream yet (encounter/aurora at 3227d76).

--- a/lib/gx/shader.cpp	2026-10-03 16:25:18
+++ b/lib/gx/shader.cpp	2026-10-03 16:25:35
@@ -363,6 +363,23 @@
   }
